<p>PerfectXML launched in 2000 as a directory and tutorial hub for XML developers. The original site documented the XML ecosystem of its day — parsers, schemas, and the tooling of a young web.</p>

<p>The 2026 edition extends that mission to today's data landscape: XML is still everywhere, and JSON, YAML and API payloads joined the party. We maintain the <a href="/411/">411 directory</a> and publish practical articles — always pointing at primary sources first.</p>

<p>PerfectXML is an independent editorial project. It is not affiliated with any standards body or vendor mentioned in the directory.</p>
